{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Kreg screw kit connects naturally to my recent wood screw purchases because it offers fasteners for joining wood.",
    "Offering several screw sizes makes sense for related construction tasks, although I would need a pocket-hole project to choose this kit."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Metal-cutting wheels, electrical connectors, and a feeler gauge require tasks I have not shown a need for; working with screws does not mean I am doing those jobs.",
    "Hose clamps serve a different fastening purpose from my wood screws and drywall anchors, while epoxy and glue require a repair need I do not currently have.",
    "Ten tubes of super glue would exceed my immediate needs; buying bulk construction fasteners does not mean I want every supply in bulk."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My construction purchases seem to have been treated as interest in almost any workshop or maintenance supply.",
    "The shared idea of fastening or repair seems to matter too much, even when the materials, connections, and tools involved are different."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of framing nails, wood screws, and drywall anchors point more specifically toward construction fastening needs.",
    "Fit matters: nail angle and collation, screw dimensions, and whether I use pocket-hole joinery determine whether a related item is useful.",
    "My medicine cups and vacuum bags reflect separate practical needs; they do not establish a need for unrelated electrical or liquid-storage supplies."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my fastening needs but stretched them into a broader workshop interest than my current tasks support."
}"}
